WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.180
Yes, we emailed you about 
that issue last week...

00:09.020 --> 00:10.820
Hot springs or Japanese sake?

00:12.580 --> 00:15.610
Yes, which one are you 
looking forward to more?

00:15.610 --> 00:16.540
Huh?

00:16.200 --> 00:18.330
<b>Ru○bu</b>

00:16.540 --> 00:18.320
Why the sudden question?

00:18.320 --> 00:22.960
Isn't the trip next week? 
We should get ready for it.

00:22.960 --> 00:23.960
Huh?

00:24.380 --> 00:28.670
No way, Senpai! Did you forget 
 the company trip's coming up?!

00:29.660 --> 00:32.010
Company...

00:32.010 --> 00:36.010
<i>I completely forgot!</i>

00:52.450 --> 00:56.780
<b>The Masterful Cat
Is Depressed Again Today</b>

02:05.980 --> 02:09.650
Can

02:05.980 --> 02:09.650
<b>A Masterful Cat Can Watch the House?</b>

02:09.850 --> 02:10.980
Can

02:09.850 --> 02:10.980
<b>A Masterful Cat Can Watch the House?</b>

02:11.710 --> 02:13.540
The company trip?!

02:13.980 --> 02:16.040
I completely forgot about it!

02:16.040 --> 02:19.110
Wait, I remember they 
passed out the schedule!

02:19.110 --> 02:22.880
Isn't this your first year 
attending, Saku-senpai?

02:22.880 --> 02:25.120
Oshiro-san told me.

02:23.260 --> 02:25.120
Blab! Blab! Blab!

02:25.520 --> 02:27.150
Yeah. That's right.

02:27.150 --> 02:29.450
We have the company trip every two years,

02:29.450 --> 02:34.020
and my cat was still a kitten 
during the last one.

02:32.750 --> 02:34.870
<i>The cat when he was a kitten.</i>

02:35.250 --> 02:36.470
I see.

02:36.470 --> 02:38.590
But you can go this time, right?

02:39.190 --> 02:43.600
I was thinking of skipping it again, 
but everyone rushed to stop me.

02:43.600 --> 02:45.890
You have to go!

02:45.890 --> 02:48.710
I won't be able to survive 
a dinner party without you, Fukuzawa!

02:48.710 --> 02:50.850
Don't abandon us!

02:51.700 --> 02:53.190
I couldn't refuse.

02:53.190 --> 02:56.810
Sounds like they'll need you there 
so they don't get drunk under the table.

02:57.610 --> 02:59.970
Well, your cat isn't a kitten anymore.

02:59.970 --> 03:02.210
I'm sure he'll be fine for a night!

03:02.210 --> 03:04.910
It might be a good idea to prepare 
two kitty litter boxes just in case...

03:05.260 --> 03:08.950
Well, he'd probably be fine 
even if I was gone for a month.

03:08.950 --> 03:11.420
<i>The cat who is no longer a kitten.</i>

03:11.820 --> 03:12.410
Huh?

03:12.410 --> 03:13.920
Oh, nothing!

03:14.600 --> 03:17.420
I haven't been on a trip in years!

03:17.420 --> 03:19.420
Ooh, Japanese sake jelly!

03:19.740 --> 03:23.010
Now that I think about it, 
I've never seen you go on any trips.

03:23.010 --> 03:23.920
Yeah...

03:23.920 --> 03:27.060
It's been a while since I've traveled 
domestically, so I'm looking forward to it!

03:27.060 --> 03:28.220
I see...

03:28.220 --> 03:30.770
Oh, I heard that place is famous!

03:31.140 --> 03:33.560
Yuri-chan, you like going 
overseas more, right?

03:33.980 --> 03:36.570
I've never left the country!

03:36.570 --> 03:39.570
You don't like traveling?

03:39.570 --> 03:42.620
No, it's not that.

03:42.980 --> 03:45.790
It's just, before I realized it...

03:45.790 --> 03:46.780
Well...

03:50.330 --> 03:54.960
My class trip in high school 
might've the last trip I went on.

03:55.530 --> 03:58.830
L-Let's have fun together, Senpai.

04:03.760 --> 04:07.470
The schedule

04:03.760 --> 04:07.470
Ru○bu magazine bought
on the way home

04:04.860 --> 04:06.780
So...

04:07.470 --> 04:10.570
I'm going to be gone for two full days.

04:10.570 --> 04:12.430
Will you be okay staying home alone?

04:12.800 --> 04:15.350
Should I buy some things for you?

04:18.230 --> 04:21.030
Well, I guess you can buy 
everything you need yourself.

04:21.880 --> 04:25.450
Then call my cell 
if you need anything.

04:25.450 --> 04:27.400
I'll try to come back home as fast as I can.

04:30.210 --> 04:33.280
You'll ask our neighbor for advice 
if you have any problems?

04:33.900 --> 04:35.330
Guess that makes sense.

04:39.090 --> 04:44.140
Th-Then I should leave some 
extra cash behind just in case.

04:45.220 --> 04:48.370
I forgot! You have an ATM card!

04:48.370 --> 04:50.580
<i>Complete management of household finances.</i>

04:51.220 --> 04:55.130
Is there anything I need to buy for the trip?

04:57.720 --> 05:01.980
Since I'm only staying one night, 
a Boston bag should be enough, right?

05:03.060 --> 05:03.790
Huh?

05:03.790 --> 05:07.390
Uh, where did I put my bag?

05:07.390 --> 05:08.740
Yukichi?

05:13.090 --> 05:17.000
Oh, you protected it with a cover. Thanks!

05:18.090 --> 05:20.310
Next are the clothes!

05:20.310 --> 05:21.750
What should I wear?

05:24.200 --> 05:25.610
Hey, Yukichi!

05:26.990 --> 05:28.310
Hmm.

05:28.760 --> 05:30.780
This'll be enough, right?

05:30.780 --> 05:32.260
Will it be cold?

05:35.560 --> 05:38.980
Huh? Did I have a cardigan like this?

05:38.980 --> 05:41.520
Did you buy this for me to wear out?

05:41.520 --> 05:43.530
Thanks, Yukichi!

05:46.080 --> 05:49.120
<i>I won't have Yukichi for two whole days.</i>

05:49.530 --> 05:51.370
<i>Will I be okay?</i>

05:58.020 --> 06:01.680
<i>Yukichi seems so calm about me leaving,</i>

06:01.680 --> 06:05.060
<i>but I can't even get packed without him.</i>

06:05.060 --> 06:07.550
<i>I might be in a lot more 
trouble than I thought.</i>

06:10.690 --> 06:13.960
<i>On top of that, if I tell him that spending 
a night without him makes me feel lonely...</i>

06:13.960 --> 06:16.060
<i>He'll definitely be exasperated again.</i>

06:42.360 --> 06:44.010
Yukichi...

06:45.620 --> 06:47.420
<i>The day of the trip.</i>

06:48.440 --> 06:50.010
Well, I'm off.

06:50.810 --> 06:54.270
<i>I feel depressed. I don't want to go.</i>

06:54.270 --> 06:58.120
<i>I won't be able to eat Yukichi's 
food for two whole days.</i>

06:58.120 --> 07:01.860
<i>It'll be easier on Yukichi since 
he won't have to cook, though.</i>

07:05.800 --> 07:07.880
What's this paper for?

07:08.730 --> 07:10.450
<i>Could it be a letter?!</i>

07:12.610 --> 07:16.370
<i>Maybe Yukichi feels lonely, too?!</i>

07:19.540 --> 07:22.540
<b>Souvenir Treasures      Moe Mountain      Saito Shop</b>

07:19.540 --> 07:22.540
<b>Garage Village      Nadeshiko Maiden</b>

07:20.040 --> 07:22.540
<i>Magazine cut-outs?!</i>

07:23.080 --> 07:28.050
I was wondering what you wanted to 
give me, but isn't this a souvenir list?!

07:29.510 --> 07:31.950
How excited are you about this trip?!

07:31.950 --> 07:35.300
You've even mapped out 
all the areas! So detailed!

07:35.640 --> 07:38.690
I don't know if I can buy all of this 
since we'll be traveling in a group!

07:39.390 --> 07:41.810
Don't expect too much!

07:41.810 --> 07:43.550
I'm going now!

08:01.260 --> 08:03.440
What's wrong with Fukuzawa?

08:03.440 --> 08:07.090
Well, she hasn't gone 
on a trip since high school.

08:07.590 --> 08:09.430
What are those cut-outs for?

08:09.740 --> 08:12.590
<i>She's researching 
all the items on the list.</i>

08:18.420 --> 08:20.620
What's wrong, Fukuzawa? Carsick?

08:20.620 --> 08:22.080
Oh! No!

08:22.080 --> 08:23.560
I'm good. Sorry!

08:23.890 --> 08:26.860
Don't get too excited 
and tire out half-way.

08:27.730 --> 08:31.280
No way. I'm not really that 
excited about the trip.

08:31.280 --> 08:32.990
No need to hide it.

08:32.990 --> 08:35.810
Everyone already knows, you know?

08:35.810 --> 08:38.370
You're so excited about the trip,

08:38.370 --> 08:41.410
that you've been staring at 
magazine cut-outs the whole time.

08:43.160 --> 08:44.950
Huh? No way! Seriously?

08:44.950 --> 08:46.790
Right on the mark, Fukuzawa?!

08:47.320 --> 08:49.590
I was half-joking!

08:55.730 --> 08:58.760
<i>The souvenir list Yukichi made for me...</i>

08:59.110 --> 09:02.770
<i>It was all things like local cosmetics 
and alcohol.</i>

09:02.770 --> 09:05.560
<i>They're all things I like...</i>

09:06.130 --> 09:10.250
<i>He must've noticed how reluctant 
I was about going on this trip.</i>

09:13.070 --> 09:17.020
I'm... I'm such a terrible pet owner!

09:17.020 --> 09:19.940
Did you forget to set up two litter boxes?

09:20.910 --> 09:23.700
We will arrive at our destination shortly.

09:23.700 --> 09:28.330
Please do not stand until the bus 
comes to a complete stop.

09:36.970 --> 09:39.180
It's so cold!

09:39.180 --> 09:40.470
<i>Yukichi...</i>

09:41.440 --> 09:45.020
<i>I wonder if he's having a relaxing break?</i>

09:50.730 --> 09:52.480
Toramaru Kitchen

10:11.050 --> 10:13.090
<i>He ran out of things to do.</i>

10:25.390 --> 10:26.990
<i>Saku's scent.</i>

10:36.610 --> 10:40.110
<b>Roll</b>

10:47.750 --> 10:53.250
<b>Roll</b>

10:52.040 --> 10:52.960
<b>Beep</b>

10:53.250 --> 10:56.510
<i>The legendary housekeeper Tama-san 
teaches again on </i>It's Afternoon<i>!</i>

10:56.510 --> 10:59.260
<i>This is the quick recipe corner 
for recipes you can even make tonight!</i>

10:59.780 --> 11:04.660
<i>Today's recipe is perfect 
as a snack with an evening drink!</i>

11:04.660 --> 11:06.230
<i>Yes, so...</i>

11:10.640 --> 11:14.300
Mommy! It's the bear rug again!

11:14.300 --> 11:16.210
You're right.

11:17.630 --> 11:19.650
<i>He ran out of things to do.</i>

11:28.110 --> 11:28.910
Huh?

11:28.910 --> 11:32.440
Yukichi-san, it's rare to see you 
shopping in the evening.

11:29.330 --> 11:32.120
Just finished work.

11:32.790 --> 11:35.180
Are you buying ingredients for dinner?

11:37.700 --> 11:39.570
<i>He seems a bit down.</i>

11:39.570 --> 11:42.220
<i>I can even tell through his cat suit.</i>

11:43.970 --> 11:48.680
<i>He only bought cat food. 
Is that his dinner?!</i>

11:49.150 --> 11:51.660
<i>Maybe that lady isn't home today?</i>

11:51.660 --> 11:54.190
<i>No, even so... Why?</i>

11:55.120 --> 11:57.440
Thank you very much.

11:57.940 --> 12:00.980
Yukichi-san! Please wait!

12:00.980 --> 12:02.670
Please take this!

12:03.800 --> 12:06.870
My manager gave me permission, 
so please take it!

12:04.360 --> 12:06.870
<b>Sample Beer</b>

12:07.960 --> 12:11.400
I hope she comes home soon.

12:12.250 --> 12:17.770
Oh, but I really don't think 
it's a good idea to eat pet food.

12:18.660 --> 12:19.540
See you.

12:33.130 --> 12:35.440
I hope she comes home soon...

12:35.940 --> 12:38.520
<i>Home soon... Home soon...</i>

12:38.520 --> 12:41.190
<i>Yukichi! Yukichi!</i>

12:44.550 --> 12:46.650
<i>Second round of the day.</i>

12:55.460 --> 12:58.790
<i>The type who vents frustration 
through cleaning.</i>

13:00.520 --> 13:02.020
Welcome!

13:04.990 --> 13:07.590
I got sauce on my hands!

13:08.810 --> 13:11.770
Oh, hold on! I might 
have some tissues on me!

13:12.100 --> 13:15.890
<b>Sterilizing 30 sheets
Alcohol Free Wipes</b>

13:12.940 --> 13:15.260
<i>Wet wipes she doesn't remember packing.</i>

13:15.890 --> 13:19.290
Ouch! I got a blister!

13:19.290 --> 13:20.750
Whoa, are you all right?!

13:20.750 --> 13:23.150
I should have brought some band-aids with me.

13:23.150 --> 13:28.160
<b>Mikuon</b>

13:24.160 --> 13:27.350
<i>Band-aids and antiseptic she 
doesn't remember packing.</i>

13:28.160 --> 13:31.660
Thank you so much, Senpai!

13:34.580 --> 13:37.350
Who're you praying to?

13:45.220 --> 13:47.380
Hmm

13:45.740 --> 13:48.450
Fukuzawa is staring really hard at something.

13:50.480 --> 13:52.370
What are you looking at?

13:52.810 --> 13:55.020
I found some local aprons.

13:55.020 --> 14:00.520
<b>Sake Brewery Master</b>

13:55.660 --> 13:58.900
Wow, you're right! 
They have all sorts of things!

13:58.900 --> 14:02.860
I'm going to ask them if the apron 
on the mannequin is for sale, too.

14:03.640 --> 14:04.900
Excuse me!

14:04.900 --> 14:06.450
We have them in stock.

14:06.450 --> 14:08.480
Would you like me to gift wrap it?

14:08.480 --> 14:10.160
No, it's for home use.

14:13.580 --> 14:16.290
<b>Sake Brewery Master</b>

14:16.540 --> 14:18.350
She looks so happy.

14:18.350 --> 14:20.820
I didn't know she was 
the Japanese apron type.

14:19.290 --> 14:22.540
<b>Sake Brewery Master</b>

14:20.820 --> 14:22.540
<i>Sorry for the wait!</i>

14:27.390 --> 14:30.500
Director? Director Narita?

14:30.500 --> 14:32.310
Please give us a hand towel!

14:32.810 --> 14:33.890
He's down?

14:33.890 --> 14:35.810
He's totally down.

14:35.810 --> 14:40.020
All right! The director has retired at 21:17!

14:40.020 --> 14:42.310
Escort him to his room!

14:42.310 --> 14:47.410
Chief Orizuka! Fukuzawa-san! 
Thank you very much!

14:42.810 --> 14:45.200
Fukuzawa, still want to drink?

14:45.200 --> 14:48.070
No, that'll be enough for me tonight.

14:47.410 --> 14:54.910
Wasshoi! Wasshoi!

14:48.430 --> 14:51.070
I'm going to get some fresh air.

14:51.070 --> 14:52.180
All right.

15:04.580 --> 15:08.250
<i>I'm so tired. It was so long.</i>

15:10.820 --> 15:16.810
<i>Lunch and dinner were delicious, 
but I want to eat Yukichi's food!</i>

15:15.510 --> 15:17.970
<b><i>Withdrawal</i></b>

15:19.250 --> 15:21.750
<i>I want to drink Yukichi's miso soup!</i>

15:20.270 --> 15:27.440
<b>God of 
Finisher Foods</b>

15:21.750 --> 15:23.380
<i>I want to eat his ochazuke!</i>

15:23.380 --> 15:27.440
<i>I can't believe I can't eat the finishers 
I always eat when I drink!</i>

15:27.440 --> 15:30.450
<i>I feel so empty! I feel so wretched!</i>

15:30.930 --> 15:32.780
There you are, Fukuzawa.

15:32.780 --> 15:35.490
Chief Orizuka! Good work today.

15:35.490 --> 15:37.700
Weren't you thrashing about just now?

15:38.440 --> 15:42.190
I-I was looking for some coins I dropped!

15:44.050 --> 15:51.000
You were drinking pretty fast today, 
so I came to make sure you didn't feel sick.

15:51.000 --> 15:53.690
Huh? Was I drinking that fast?

15:53.690 --> 15:55.850
It looked like you were 
trying to drown yourself in it.

15:55.850 --> 16:00.230
N-No way! I don't drink like that anymore!

16:00.230 --> 16:03.520
I thought you would crash 
before the director.

16:03.520 --> 16:05.980
I-I'm totally fine!

16:07.670 --> 16:09.700
Come to think of it, how's your cat?

16:10.740 --> 16:12.300
What's wrong?

16:12.620 --> 16:15.350
It's because you asked me 
about my cat so suddenly!

16:16.340 --> 16:18.910
Did something happen to him? Sorry.

16:18.910 --> 16:20.860
Nothing happened to him!

16:20.860 --> 16:23.010
He's taking care of the house while I'm gone!

16:23.010 --> 16:26.750
Is it okay to leave a cat alone overnight?

16:28.730 --> 16:31.840
My cat definitely has no problem with it.

16:32.990 --> 16:36.010
I think it's actually easier 
on him if I'm not home.

16:36.490 --> 16:38.380
I'm sure that's not true.

16:38.380 --> 16:41.270
They say that cats attach 
themselves to the home,

16:41.270 --> 16:44.600
but the black cat we used to have...

16:45.680 --> 16:46.600
Fukuzawa?

16:50.970 --> 16:52.110
Really?

16:53.050 --> 16:55.610
This is Fukuzawa Saku's room, right?

16:55.610 --> 16:56.350
Ye...

16:56.350 --> 16:57.470
Yes!

16:57.470 --> 17:01.120
Huh? Saku-senpai? What happened to her?

17:01.660 --> 17:05.230
As you can see, I had to carry her here 
because she's completely drunk.

17:06.080 --> 17:09.120
Y-Y-You carried her here like that?

17:09.120 --> 17:10.920
What else was I going to do?

17:11.690 --> 17:14.090
Hey! Get a hold of yourself, Fukuzawa!

17:13.470 --> 17:14.920
<b>Yukata falling apart</b>

17:13.470 --> 17:14.920
<b>Slippers lost</b>

17:14.920 --> 17:17.000
Thank you for your hard work...

17:20.430 --> 17:22.600
<b>Snore</b>

17:20.910 --> 17:24.490
He left her here, but what should we do?

17:23.430 --> 17:25.600
<b>Snore</b>

17:24.490 --> 17:27.400
She doesn't have alcohol poisoning, does she?

17:26.440 --> 17:27.400
<b>Snore</b>

17:27.400 --> 17:31.900
The way she's sleeping and 
the color of her face says otherwise.

17:31.900 --> 17:33.400
Whoa! She woke up!

17:33.400 --> 17:36.140
A-Are you all right, Senpai?

17:37.190 --> 17:38.910
She's looking for something?

17:39.660 --> 17:43.260
Water?! You should drink some water, Senpai!

17:43.260 --> 17:44.660
No, my phone.

17:45.700 --> 17:46.920
Found it.

17:47.770 --> 17:49.670
I'm going to call my cat at home.

17:50.120 --> 17:52.760
This is bad! Fukuzawa's totally lost it!

17:52.760 --> 17:54.380
Do we need to call for an ambulance?

17:54.380 --> 17:57.430
Senpai! Please get a hold of yourself!

18:01.500 --> 18:04.060
<i>As usual, a cat that 
doesn't turn on the lights.</i>

18:10.420 --> 18:12.070
<i>Oh, Yukichi?</i>

18:12.070 --> 18:16.080
<i>It's me! Did you eat dinner properly?</i>

18:14.830 --> 18:17.090
<i>Did Fukuzawa really call her cat?!</i>

18:17.090 --> 18:18.840
Senpai is way too drunk.

18:18.840 --> 18:21.570
I got you souvenirs!

18:22.740 --> 18:26.080
I want to eat a meal at home.

18:26.370 --> 18:28.810
<i>I'm lonely without you.</i>

18:41.220 --> 18:44.720
<b>Purr</b>

18:49.250 --> 18:51.730
<i>S-See you later! Good night!</i>

18:51.730 --> 18:54.010
She's already done?

18:54.010 --> 18:55.430
Oshiro-san!

18:56.860 --> 18:58.750
She's suddenly rolling around!

18:58.750 --> 19:01.110
Are you all right, Saku-senpai?!

19:01.110 --> 19:03.580
My cat's so cute, it hurts!

19:03.580 --> 19:05.170
It's terminal. So scary!

19:05.170 --> 19:07.850
This is a common problem for cat owners!

19:09.940 --> 19:11.320
She fell asleep!

19:11.320 --> 19:12.400
Senpai, water!

19:12.400 --> 19:14.880
You haven't even brushed your teeth yet!

19:54.780 --> 19:59.460
Well, I experienced something 
really interesting last night.

19:59.460 --> 20:01.100
I'm sorry.

20:01.530 --> 20:04.180
Don't be so mean, Oshiro-san!

20:04.760 --> 20:09.430
It's so weird to see Saku-senpai 
get that drunk and have a hangover!

20:09.740 --> 20:12.490
I'm sure you weren't feeling well yesterday!

20:12.490 --> 20:15.440
No. That's not it, actually.

20:15.790 --> 20:18.220
But sorry for making you worry.

20:18.220 --> 20:21.280
Are you sure you don't need 
to go see a doctor?

20:23.060 --> 20:24.510
Yeah, I'm fine.

20:24.510 --> 20:27.240
I'll get better once I get home 
and eat something.

20:27.660 --> 20:29.400
There's still half a day left.

20:44.370 --> 20:46.650
<i>I'm finally home.</i>

20:47.230 --> 20:51.770
<i>I haven't traveled this far 
with a hangover in a long time!</i>

20:53.570 --> 20:56.370
<i>I wonder how Yukichi's doing?</i>

21:00.720 --> 21:04.660
<i>Maybe he'll be waiting for me at the door?</i>

21:05.200 --> 21:09.280
<i>Or maybe he'll sigh, 
exasperated that I'm hungover.</i>

21:18.380 --> 21:20.300
I'm home, Yukichi!

23:06.940 --> 23:17.540
<b>Next Episode</b>

23:07.580 --> 23:09.490
<i>A masterful cat knows.</i>

23:09.870 --> 23:12.310
<i>It is important to do strength 
training while dieting.</i>

23:12.310 --> 23:16.370
<i>Muscle burns more calories, 
making it harder to gain fat.</i>

23:16.370 --> 23:20.210
<i>Next episode: "A Masterful Cat 
Also Cares about Health."</i>

23:17.540 --> 23:21.960
Can

23:17.540 --> 23:21.960
<b>A Masterful Cat Also Cares about Health</b>

23:20.210 --> 23:21.540
<i>Naturally.</i>
